        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-07-14T22:28:58.758Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Got to listen to most of this at home!</p>\n<p>Adam and I had the same idea at the start of the episode. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>The moment she called Painstake her daughter, I immediately began thinking of Ashdia as “Momstake” XD</p>\n<p>Wow, Darkstrife and Painstake fighting <em>again?</em> It’s like a two-for-one!</p>\n<p>Love this musical interlude.</p>\n<p>Oh, so that’s what Betrayer Painstake’s deal is! We need to do more topics based on new DE cards.</p>\n<p>Sushi?! What happened to the sandwich bag??</p>\n<p>I don’t often say this, but this has been a fantastic letters section!</p>\n<p>God, and this episode has somehow given me TWO ideas for villains. Literally how.</p>\n<p>Looking at the image of Ashdia as they describe her, yeah, this is a really awesome looking character.</p>\n<p>Ooh, I also was once a Prairie Home Companion enjoyer. Anyway, also loving this outro, this has been an all-around great episode. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
        "post_number": 2,
